{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/902679-solar-danmaku-charms-colorfull-thrown-charms-3rd-edition","id":902679,"title":"Solar Danmaku Charms (Colorfull Thrown Charms) 3rd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T06:50:00-07:00","id":902679,"title":"Solar Danmaku Charms (Colorfull Thrown Charms) 3rd Edition","content":"So, after some thinking I decided to write few additional Charms for Thrown, as unfortunately at this moment Thrown narratively works perfectly for silent assassins \u2013 but not for many other types of characters. Charms here are based on Danmaku style games (Touhou especially) and their stylish displays of powerful, yet beautiful and very visible attacks. Please evaluate and comment honestly.<br /> These Charm are cannibalization of Aquamarine Bullets of Friendship Style, my Sidereal Martial Art written for 2,5 Edition. I would also like to use this place to ask \u2013 what do you think about martial arts style with similar effects and added theme of friendship though defeat as Celestial Martial Arts? Because it will take few years until we get Sidereals and I\u2019m thinking about rewriting my style as Celestial before then.<br /> <br /> <b>Blades of the Sun</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp ; Mins: Thrown 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Cascade of Cutting Terror<br /> Looking for weapons or scavenging them is below Chosen of the Sun. Why scavenge weapons from enemies, when you can call upon your own birthright to shape blades from Essence itself?<br /> Upon activating this Charm hundreds of throwing weapons start circling around Solar, all of them constantly moving, but all always within his grasp. Those weapon are not real, only a mere phantasms of blades crafted from all colors of sunlight \u2013 at least, while not held or thrown by Solar. When this Charm is Active, Solar is considered to always have a weapon Readied as long as she has at least one hand empty \u2013 she can choose any weapon summoned by this Charm. She can Reflexively change Readied weapon with any other weapon summoned by this Charm, or Ready another one after throwing first. While Solar holds weapon summoned by this Charm, such weapon becomes real in every way and remains in this state until striking enemy upon being thrown or if it is separated from Solar for more than One Action. In such situation weapon disappears and then materializes again among hundreds of other phantasmal weapons encircling Martial Artist.<br /> Upon learning this Charm Solar must choose [Essence/2, rounded up] templates of weapons he will be able to summon with this Charm. He can add new templates (but not change previous) upon raising in Essence. When activating this Charm, Martial Artist can choose to summon all or only some of the templates available to him. This Charms allows creation of any base quality mundane weapons.<br /> Upon reaching Thrown 5, Essence 3, all weapons created by this Charm are automatically upgraded to their artificial versions.<br /> <i>Comment: Glorious Solar Sabre for Throwing Weapons (or old edition Fiery Solar Chakram).</i><br /> <br /> <b>Wondrous Missile Curtain Pattern </b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp ; Mins: Thrown 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Blades of the Sun<br /> As the Solar throws her phantasmal weapons around her, they move as fast as if creating new galaxy of light. Upon activation, shimmering light encircles Solar, taking form of constellation of miniature suns and light beams orbiting her person at enormous speed.<br /> When this Charm is active, Solar rolls (Essence) dies on each turn to inflict withering damage on all other characters within close range. At Essence 4+ this Charm works up to short range. Against enemies in Initiative Crash and trivial opponents this Charm constitutes an environmental hazard (Damage (Solar\u2019s Essence) L/action, Difficulty (Solar\u2019s Essence+2) ) resisted with (Dexterity+Dodge). Solar may reflexively choose whether or not these projectiles inflict lethal damage on character to character basis; if she chooses to inflict bashing damage, no damage from this hazard can injure a character further than Incapacitated. Solar may exclude every person to whom he has some positive Intimacy from suffering effects of this Charm.<br /> Additionally, it becomes difficult to target the Solar through the shining lights, as their colorful display obscure the sight, and their physical power changes course of blows; attacks suffer an penalty of [Solar\u2019s Essence, round up]<br /> <i>Comment: Based on 3RD Edition anima flux, 2nd Edition Orbital Impact Storm, Inugami Touhou-themed 2ed Solar Thrown Charm and my homebrew Bullet-Patterns of Love from my Aquamarine Bullets of Friendship Style.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blades-as-Shields Method</b><br /> Cost: (+3m) ; Mins: Thrown 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Blades of the Sun<br /> Upon learning this Charm, Solar\u2019s phantasmal blades take on more material form, moving around Solar to stop all danger to her by swatting attacks away.<br /> This Charm is permanent upgrade to Blades of the Sun, allowing Solar to increase its cost by 3 motes when activating it and giving it additional effects. As long as Blades of the Sun is active, Solar can parry all attacks as if she was wielding medium artificial weapon with Shield tags, using her (Dexterity + Melee) or (Dexterity + Thrown) dice pools. She can use additional Melee Charms to support this parry only if she is using her (Melee) dice pool. Additionally, she is considered to be always behind Heavy Cover as long as Blades of the Sun is active.<br /> <br /> <b>Blade Following Blade Approach</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp ; Mins: Thrown 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shower of Deadly Blades<br /> Calling upon her inner eye and her ultimate speed, Solar throws blade after blade, stopping enemies in their tracks.<br /> The Solar may draw multiple thrown weapons and attack a single target repeatedly, launching multiple withering attacks until she either misses or crashes her opponent. Blade following Blade Approach can only be used within short or close range, and can\u2019t be used on targets already in crash. Used against a battle group, the Solar attacks until she misses or depletes the group\u2019s Magnitude.<br /> At Essence 4+, the Solar gains one point of temporary Willpower when she crashes a foe with this attack.<br /> <i>Comment: Just Revolving Bow Technique for Thrown.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Spark of Solar Mastery</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 3a, 1wp ; Mins: Thrown 5, Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Fiery Solar Chakram, Wondrous Missile Curtain Pattern<br /> Taking upon her positive feelings and shaping them into weapon to protect her friends, Solar gather her anima into tremendous display of her prowess, throwing pure beam of light and energy against her foes.<br /> The attack ignores the range of her weapon, and can be made from medium or long range without an aim action, or extreme range with an aim action. Solar gains full dice benefits of having used a full Thrown Excellency on this attack. The Solar must have higher Initiative than her target to use this attack; the conjured beam does not use the Solar\u2019s Initiative to do damage, but instead has a raw damage equal to her current temporary Willpower multiplied by one or the rating of any positive Intimacy she is trying to uphold or protect. Any target between Solar and her main target with Initiative lower than Solar is also hit, but only with raw damage equal to her current temporary Willpower.<br /> Solar may reflexively choose whether or not that beam inflict lethal damage on character to character basis; if she chooses to inflict bashing damage, no damage from this hazard can injure a character further than Incapacitated. Solar may exclude every person to whom he has some positive Intimacy from suffering effects of this Charm.<br /> Using this Charm sets her anima back to the dim level, and in order to use it again, the player must make three separate stunts in which her anima grows while she begins to produce the strength to unleash another Glorious Spark of Solar Mastery. These stunts must always be related to the Intimacy used to unleash Glorious Spark of Solar Mastery.<br /> <i>Comment: Parts of Fiery Solar Chakram, Solar Spike and Cascade of Cutting Terror combined to form new Charm.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":11704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","user":"Daerian","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:03:37-07:00","id":902693,"title":"","content":"Interesting charms there - especially the last one. Requiring 3 stunts before you can re-activate it... hmm - interesting way of balancing it, especially when its dmg is how much temp willpower you have left x the potency of the intimacy of what you're trying to defend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:40:04-07:00","id":902710,"title":"","content":"It looks intriguing , now make me wonder what kind of off the chart charms, we are going to see in the backer charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:46:45-07:00","id":903572,"title":"","content":"Just imagine the sight of two Solars doing a <i>Touhou </i>battle. The mind boggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 05-30-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:44:51-07:00","id":910737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/902679-solar-danmaku-charms-colorfull-thrown-charms-3rd-edition#post902679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after some thinking I decided to write few additional Charms for Thrown, as unfortunately at this moment Thrown narratively works perfectly for silent assassins \u2013 but not for many other types of characters. Charms here are based on Danmaku style games (Touhou especially) and their stylish displays of powerful, yet beautiful and very visible attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>A noble goal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These Charm are cannibalization of Aquamarine Bullets of Friendship Style, my Sidereal Martial Art written for 2,5 Edition. I would also like to use this place to ask \u2013 what do you think about martial arts style with similar effects and added theme of friendship though defeat as Celestial Martial Arts? Because it will take few years until we get Sidereals and I\u2019m thinking about rewriting my style as Celestial before then. </div> </div> </div>Crane Style offers one avenue of &quot;friendship through defeat&quot; already, with the martial artist &quot;proving&quot; themselves worthy of trust by showing kindness and concern for the opponent in trying to talk with them, reason with them, and sparing their life.<br /> <br /> I've made more progress on my &quot;Pacifist Run&quot; Style, which places even more on an emphasis of talking out one's problems without resorting to lethal violence... or any violence at all.<br /> <br /> I don't think a non-Sidereal Style can get more social than that. Crane integrates certain social mechanics into its counterattacks but doesn't exactly have social Charms, and my Pursuit of Peace Style is composed of Charms that make talking while defending yourself easier without actually making you more persuasive in the way that social Charms would.<br /> <br /> Then there's Black Claw Style, which seeks to trap people into liking the martial artist under false pretenses, but its seduction is still defensive rather than aggressive in that it cannot seduce anyone unless the stylist is attacked.<br /> <br /> A Style which is more aggressive than Black Claw or Crane Style and yet still allows you to beat someone until they love you for it... honestly speaking, that would be the sado-masochistic Laughing Wounds Style, with its chains and whips and leather.<br /> <br /> But don't fall into the trap of relying on martial artist for everything. There's definitely always the option of employing your native social Charms together with your native combat Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I really like the concept of Blades of the Sun; definitely something equivalent to Glorious Solar Saber, and yet different in a way that is interesting and relevant to how the needs of Thrown are different from the needs of Melee.<br /> <br /> I like where the Charm is placed in regards to the canon Charms, and I like how you used it as the bridge to Wondrous Missile Curtain Pattern.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that you credited me for WMCP, and I appreciate your adaptations for 3rdEd.<br /> <br /> Blades-as-Shields Method was the absolutely necessary follow-up.<br /> <br /> Blade Following Blade Approach is cool.<br /> <br /> The Master Spark was mandatory, but I'm not qualified to speak on how well it is balanced or executed. I need to study it more.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the &quot;merciful&quot; effects of these Charms could belong in an upgrade Charm instead, but it really depends on whether enough of the inspirational material involves Solar-like characters killing people with their thrown bolts of light.<br /> <br /> Lina Inverse's &quot;master spark&quot; is explicitly sorcery. Namely, Death Ray. Whereas the chi-bolts of Dragon Ball never kill anyone unless the hero means to kill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:22:08-07:00","id":910759,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for comment and opinions! :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:42:59-07:00","id":910833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/902679-solar-danmaku-charms-colorfull-thrown-charms-3rd-edition?p=910759#post910759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot for comment and opinions! :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanted to respond as soon as you posted, but was too busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:00:00-07:00","id":910906,"title":"","content":"One thing you are missing is the &quot;Bomb&quot; option, where you take Wondrous Missile Curtain Pattern and cancel it prematurely by turning it into a brief explosion. <br /> <br /> Also, you should put spaces between your paragraphs, to avoid the appearance of Wall Of Text. Double-spaces between Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-09-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}